# docs §9.1: demandsVersion is a SHA-256 hash over these files' raw bytes,
# and must match byte-for-byte between src/data/learn/demands/ (this repo)
# and backend/data/learn/ (a separate repo, synced via
# `npm run learn:sync-backend`). core.autocrlf on Windows would otherwise
# convert LF -> CRLF on checkout here but not necessarily identically in the
# backend repo, silently breaking hash parity depending on platform. Force
# LF so the checked-out bytes are the same on every machine.
src/data/learn/demands/*.json text eol=lf
src/data/learn/demandsManifest.ts text eol=lf
